  "question": "Do exact C-II-N crossings from 42 through 48 ke support a historically plausible interior whole-ke selection layer, and does an independent calendrical witness preserve a daily interpolation mechanism without collapsing that mechanism into the exact 1578 Sanming/Yueling fingerprint?",
  "answer": "YES FOR THE INTERIOR 42-48 THRESHOLD MECHANISM AND FOR AN INDEPENDENT DAILY-INTERPOLATION CONTROL; NO FOR A UNIVERSAL FLOOR RULE OR THE EXACT SANMING/YUELING PARENT. Direct no-OCR re-collation places the 42..48 integer crossings between days 20/21, 33/34, 42/43, 50/51, 58/59, 66/67 and 73/74. These interior transitions are all consistent with a fraction-discard/floor-like threshold layer, but C-II-N reaches only about 58.6332 ke at the summer endpoint while received whole-ke tables display 59/41, so a global floor/truncation rule remains disproved as an overclaim. Xuxiu 1061's Ming-manuscript reproduction of Taiyi Tongzong Baojian directly preserves a daily sunrise-difference algorithm; a 2025 scholarly collation independently compares this mechanism with the 1216 Gengwu Yuanli. The Taiyi work's 1303 self-preface does not physically date every calendrical layer, and none of this resolves Sanming/Yueling's anomalous Yushui post-day-4 fingerprint.",
